{"rsid":2580,"house":"Rajya Sabha","name":"Shri Nagendra Ray","reviewed_at":"2026-10-29T22:19:46.654Z","sections":{"questions":{"source":"https://rsdoc.nic.in/Question/GetMeber_Question?mpcode=2580","status":"available","total":1,"source_total":1,"records":[{"mp_code":2580,"qslno":313715,"qtitle":"Grant of notional increment to the employees","qtype":"UNSTARRED ","ans_date":"03.04.2025","adate":"2025-04-03T00:00:00","shri":"Shri      ","qno":3798,"name":"Nagendra Ray                            ","min_name":"PERSONNEL,PUBLIC GRIEVANCES AND PENSIONS","qn_text":"(a) whether Government has issued orders for grant of notional increment on 1st July/1st January to the employees who retired from Central Government service on 30th June/31st December respectively for the purpose of calculating their pensionary benefits;  \r\n(b) if so, the date from which this order has been applicable and implemented; and\r\n(c) whether the implementing of the order is applicable to the employees who have retired prior to 2023?","ans_text":null,"ses_no":267,"depc":58,"status":"Answered  ","P_flag":"Y","files":"https://sansad.in/getFile/annex/267/AU3798_7wLrCr.pdf?source=pqars","hindifiles":"https://sansad.in/getFile/qhindi/267/AU3798_7wLrCr.pdf?source=pqars","eng_file_name":"AU3798_7wLrCr.pdf","hindi_file_name":"AU3798_7wLrCr.pdf","eng_file_dsp":"/getFile/annex/267/AU3798_7wLrCr.pdf?source=pqars","hindi_file_dsp":"/getFile/qhindi/267/AU3798_7wLrCr.pdf?source=pqars","min_code":0,"supp":null}]},"special_mentions":{"source":"https://rsdoc.nic.in/memberGetdata/Get_SpecialMentionmemberwise?mpcode=2580","status":"available","total":4,"source_total":4,"records":[{"mp_code":2580,"mp_name":"Shri                Nagendra                                                    Ray                                                         ","sr_no":176,"subject":"Demand for re-establishment, operationalization and upgradation of Cooch Behar Heritage Airport.","sess_no":270,"SM_Text":"<p><p class=MsoNormal style=margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;\r\nmargin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:\r\n-1.0in;line-height:normal><span lang=EN-US style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Times New Roman\",serif>Shri Nagendra Ray: </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style=margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;line-height:normal><span lang=EN-US style=font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:\"Times New Roman\",serif>I seek to draw attention of the Government\r\ntowards the need for the re-establishment and operationalization of the Cooch\r\nBehar Heritage Airport, and its upgradation into a dual-use civil and military\r\nairbase, in the larger interest of regional connectivity and economic\r\ndevelopment defending national security from any hostile countries like China,\r\nPakistan, Bangladesh and other countries for religious terrorist activities. It\r\nis a known fact that China and Bangladesh are targeting Siliguri Corridor as\r\nthe ?eye of a bird? from the Lalmonirhat Military airbase in Bangladesh to\r\ndisconnect North East from our Country.The Cooch Behar Heritage Airport holds\r\nhistorical significance and is strategically located in North Bengal, close to\r\ninternational borders. This airport had an outstanding role during 1st &amp;\r\n2nd world wars in 1914 and 1939. Given its geographical importance, revival and\r\ndevelopment of this airport would greatly strengthen air connectivity in a\r\nregion. Re-establishing civil aviation operations from Cooch Behar would\r\nsignificantly improve regional air connectivity, promote tourism, facilitate\r\nbusiness activities, and provide faster access to medical and emergency\r\nservices. At the same time, operationalization of the airport as a military\r\nairbase would enhance strategic preparedness and logistical capability in this\r\nsensitive border region, complementing national defence objectives.??? I also\r\nrequest that the airport be upgraded with modern aviation infrastructure,\r\nnavigational and communication systems, safety and security installations, and\r\nsupporting road and utility connectivity. Development of allied infrastructure\r\nwould also generate employment opportunities and catalyze socio-economic growth\r\nin the region.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal align=right style=margin-bottom:0in;text-align:right;\r\nline-height:normal><span lang=EN-US style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:DVOT-Yogesh>(ENDS)</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style=margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal><span\r\nlang=EN-US style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:DVOT-Yogesh></p>","Admis_Sno":0,"Made":"y","made_Date":"25/03/2026","Ministry":"CIVIL AVIATION","dt_iss":null,"proposed_dt":null,"MIN_NO":"37","Permitted":"y","Date_Permission":"-         ","sno_made":176,"dt_final":null,"reply":"No Reply","made_date_compare":"2026-03-25T00:00:00"},{"mp_code":2580,"mp_name":"Shri                Nagendra                                                    Ray                                                         ","sr_no":38,"subject":"Demand for conferment of Bharat Ratna on Maharaja Jagaddipendra Narayan Bhup Bahadur of Cooch Behar.","sess_no":266,"SM_Text":null,"Admis_Sno":0,"Made":"y","made_Date":"04/12/2024","Ministry":"HOME AFFAIRS","dt_iss":null,"proposed_dt":null,"MIN_NO":"33","Permitted":"y","Date_Permission":"-         ","sno_made":38,"dt_final":null,"reply":"No Reply","made_date_compare":"2024-12-04T00:00:00"},{"mp_code":2580,"mp_name":"Shri                Nagendra                                                    Ray                                                         ","sr_no":81,"subject":"REQUEST FOR CONSIDERATION OF DEMAND OF THE GREATER COOCH BEHAR PEOPLE’S ASSOCIATION FOR FORMATION OF GREATER COOCH BEHAR AS UNION TERRITORY","sess_no":265,"SM_Text":"<p><p class=MsoNormal style=margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:normal><span lang=EN-IN style=font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:DVOT-Yogesh>Shri Nagendra Ray: Sir, there has been a long pending\r\ndemand of the Greater Cooch Behar People?s Association since the year </span><span\r\nlang=HI style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:DVOT-Yogesh>2015</span><span\r\nlang=EN-IN style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:DVOT-Yogesh> for formation of\r\nGreater Cooch Behar as a Union Territory by carving it out of the State of West\r\nBengal. The Association has made a number of representations to the Government\r\nin the past to realize aspirations of its people.? This Association has been\r\nagainst merger of the then Cooch Behar with the States of West Bengal and?\r\nAssam as they considered it illegal, unconstitutional and against the wishes of\r\nthe locals. For the knowledge of my colleagues here, I would like to mention\r\nthat the then Government was aware of the ground situation that merger of\r\nGreater Cooch Behar with West Bengal and Assam is very sensitive because of violation\r\nof the Instrument of Accession of State of Cooch Behar signed between Maharaja\r\nShri Jagaddipendra Narayan Bhup Bahadur and Lord Mountbatten, Governor General,\r\nDominion Govt. of India, on </span><span lang=HI style=font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:DVOT-Yogesh>9</span><sup><span lang=EN-IN style=font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:DVOT-Yogesh>th</span></sup><span lang=EN-IN style=font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:DVOT-Yogesh>? August, </span><span lang=HI style=font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:DVOT-Yogesh>1947</span><span lang=EN-IN style=font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:DVOT-Yogesh> and Agreement Annexure ? ?A? made on </span><span\r\nlang=HI style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:DVOT-Yogesh>28</span><sup><span\r\nlang=EN-IN style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:DVOT-Yogesh>th</span></sup><span\r\nlang=EN-IN style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:DVOT-Yogesh>? and </span><span\r\nlang=HI style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:DVOT-Yogesh>30</span><sup><span\r\nlang=EN-IN style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:DVOT-Yogesh>th</span></sup><span\r\nlang=EN-IN style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:DVOT-Yogesh>? August, </span><span\r\nlang=HI style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:DVOT-Yogesh>1949. </span><span\r\nlang=EN-IN style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:DVOT-Yogesh>Interestingly Cooch\r\nBehar was shown as ?C? category State in the First Schedule of the Constitution\r\nadopted by Constituent Assembly on </span><span lang=HI style=font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:DVOT-Yogesh>26</span><sup><span lang=EN-IN style=font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:DVOT-Yogesh>th</span></sup><span lang=EN-IN style=font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:DVOT-Yogesh> November, </span><span lang=HI style=font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:DVOT-Yogesh>1949. </span><span lang=EN-IN style=font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:DVOT-Yogesh>Therefore, I would sincerely request Hon?ble Home\r\nMinister to undo the injustice done to people of Cooch Behar by carving out it\r\nas a separate Union Territory. </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal align=right style=margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;\r\ntext-align:right;line-height:normal><span lang=EN-IN style=font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:DVOT-Yogesh>(Ends)</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style=margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:normal><b><span lang=EN-IN style=font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:DVOT-Yogesh></p>","Admis_Sno":0,"Made":"y","made_Date":"24/07/2024","Ministry":"HOME AFFAIRS","dt_iss":null,"proposed_dt":null,"MIN_NO":"33","Permitted":"y","Date_Permission":"-         ","sno_made":49,"dt_final":null,"reply":"No Reply","made_date_compare":"2024-07-24T00:00:00"},{"mp_code":2580,"mp_name":"Shri                Nagendra                                                    Ray                                                         ","sr_no":395,"subject":"Demand to conduct a comprehensive review for restoration of the original character and position of the Library as the Cooch Behar National Library in the larger interest of the Kshatriya Rajbanshi community","sess_no":265,"SM_Text":"<p><p class=MsoNormal style=margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:normal><b><span style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:DVOT-Yogesh>Shri\r\nNagendra Ray:</span></b><span style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:DVOT-Yogesh>\r\nSir, Historically speaking, the establishment of the Cooch Behar National\r\nLibrary at Cooch Behar Palace dates back to the year 1870.? This Library has\r\ngreat heritage character and position among the local people of the Kshastriya\r\nRajbanshi community because of cultural and ethnical bond and values. It has a\r\nhuge collection of various types of rare books, Journals, magazines,\r\nmanuscripts, periodicals,? etc.?? The historical library was later re-named as\r\nthe North Bengal State library and? is situated in the heart of Cooch Behar\r\nTown.? It is important to know that after the merger of Cooch Behar with the\r\nIndian Dominion, the library was accorded A -Category Status. Later it was\r\nrenamed as North Bengal state library by West Bengal Govt. and in the process it\r\ngot B category status on 1st April, 1969. I humbly request the Central\r\nGovernment to conduct a comprehensive review of the situation and order\r\nrestoration of the original character and position of the Library as the Cooch\r\nBehar National Library in the larger interest of the Kshatriya Rajbanshi\r\ncommunity.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal align=right style=margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;\r\ntext-align:right;line-height:normal><span style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\r\nDVOT-Yogesh>(Ends)</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style=margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:\r\nnormal><b><span style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:DVOT-Yogesh></p>","Admis_Sno":0,"Made":"y","made_Date":"06/08/2024","Ministry":"CULTURE","dt_iss":null,"proposed_dt":null,"MIN_NO":"86","Permitted":"y","Date_Permission":"-         ","sno_made":172,"dt_final":null,"reply":"No Reply","made_date_compare":"2024-08-06T00:00:00"}]},"committees":{"source":"https://integration.rajyasabha.digital/committee-integration/api/v1/web/mp/Get_Committee_DetailMemberwise?mpcode=2580","status":"available","total":1,"source_total":1,"records":[{"memname":"Nagendra Ray","comname":"Rural Development","comm_code":33,"comm_code_old":"33","frmdate":"2025-09-26 00:00:00","date":"26/09/2025","type":"Member","house":"Rajya Sabha"}]},"attendance_sessions":{"source":"https://sansad.in/api_rs/member/attendance/sessions?mpCode=2580","status":"available","total":11,"source_total":11,"records":[{"id":3423,"startDate":"2026-07-20 00:00:00.0","endDate":"2026-08-13 00:00:00.0","sessionNo":271,"description":"MonsoonSession"},{"id":3422,"startDate":"2026-01-28 00:00:00.0","endDate":"2026-04-18 00:00:00.0","sessionNo":270,"description":"BudgetSession"},{"id":3421,"startDate":"2025-12-01 00:00:00.0","endDate":"2025-12-19 00:00:00.0","sessionNo":269,"description":"WinterSession"},{"id":3420,"startDate":"2025-07-21 00:00:00.0","endDate":"2025-08-21 00:00:00.0","sessionNo":268,"description":"MonsoonSession"},{"id":3419,"startDate":"2025-01-31 00:00:00.0","endDate":"2025-04-04 00:00:00.0","sessionNo":267,"description":"BudgetSession"},{"id":3418,"startDate":"2024-11-25 00:00:00.0","endDate":"2024-12-20 00:00:00.0","sessionNo":266,"description":"WinterSession"},{"id":3417,"startDate":"2024-07-22 00:00:00.0","endDate":"2024-08-09 00:00:00.0","sessionNo":265,"description":"MonsoonSession"},{"id":3416,"startDate":"2024-06-27 00:00:00.0","endDate":"2024-07-03 00:00:00.0","sessionNo":264,"description":"SpecialSession"},{"id":3415,"startDate":"2024-01-31 00:00:00.0","endDate":"2024-02-10 00:00:00.0","sessionNo":263,"description":"BudgetSession"},{"id":3414,"startDate":"2023-12-04 00:00:00.0","endDate":"2023-12-21 00:00:00.0","sessionNo":262,"description":"WinterSession"},{"id":3409,"startDate":"2023-09-18 00:00:00.0","endDate":"2023-09-21 00:00:00.0","sessionNo":261,"description":"SpecialSession"}]},"t